<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Limitation</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While our study provides a comprehensive characterization of probability-based objectives across the model-capability continuum, several limitations remain. First, we did not extend our experiments to excessively large models (e.g., 30B–70B parameters) due to computational resource constraints. Second, our framework for assessing initial model capability, via mean predicted probability and domain priors, serves as a first attempt, and future work may design more principled or fine-grained measures of capability, specifically tailored for SFT. Third, although our analysis spans the model-strong and model-weak ends extensively, our exploration of the intermediate region remains relatively limited. While our work serves as the pioneering study and we identify its neutrality in objective comparisons, a more careful study of this middle ground could yield deeper insights and potentially inspire adaptive or hybrid strategies that bridge the two extremes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proofs for Sec. <a href="#S2" title="2 A Unified Categorization of SFT Training Objectives ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gradient Shape)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be differentiable and nonincreasing.
Consider the objective in Eq. <a href="#S2.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 2 A Unified Categorization of SFT Training Objectives ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, whose step-<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> contribution depends on the correct-class probability <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t,y}=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{t})_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t,y}=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{t})_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> only through <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p_{t,y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p_{t,y})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the gradient of <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the logits at step <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,i}}\;=\;s_{f}\!\left(p_{t,y}\right)\,\bigl(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i}\bigr),\qquad\text{where}\quad s_{f}(p)\;\triangleq\;-\,f^{\prime}(p)\,p\;\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,i}}\;=\;s_{f}\!\left(p_{t,y}\right)\,\bigl(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i}\bigr),\qquad\text{where}\quad s_{f}(p)\;\triangleq\;-\,f^{\prime}(p)\,p\;\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, for the correct class <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,y}}=s_{f}(p_{t,y})\,(1-p_{t,y})\;=\;W_{f}(p_{t,y}),\qquad W_{f}(p)\;\triangleq\;-\,f^{\prime}(p)\,p\,(1-p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,y}}=s_{f}(p_{t,y})\,(1-p_{t,y})\;=\;W_{f}(p_{t,y}),\qquad W_{f}(p)\;\triangleq\;-\,f^{\prime}(p)\,p\,(1-p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t,i}=\exp(z_{t,i})/\sum_{j}\exp(z_{t,j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t,i}=\exp(z_{t,i})/\sum_{j}\exp(z_{t,j})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The softmax Jacobian gives, for all <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial p_{t,y}}{\partial z_{t,i}}=p_{t,y}\,(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial p_{t,y}}{\partial z_{t,i}}=p_{t,y}\,(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the step-<math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> loss is <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p_{t,y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p_{t,y})</annotation></semantics></math>, the chain rule yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,i}}=f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\;\frac{\partial p_{t,y}}{\partial z_{t,i}}=f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\,p_{t,y}\,(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i})=\bigl(-f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\,p_{t,y}\bigr)\,(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,i}}=f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\;\frac{\partial p_{t,y}}{\partial z_{t,i}}=f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\,p_{t,y}\,(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i})=\bigl(-f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\,p_{t,y}\bigr)\,(\delta_{i,y}-p_{t,i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(p)=-f^{\prime}(p)\,p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(p)=-f^{\prime}(p)\,p</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing, <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(p)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(p)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}(p)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}(p)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The displayed formula then follows, and for <math id="A5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=y</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain
<math id="A5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,y}}=s_{f}(p_{t,y})(1-p_{t,y})=-f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\,p_{t,y}(1-p_{t,y})=W_{f}(p_{t,y})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{f}}{\partial z_{t,y}}=s_{f}(p_{t,y})(1-p_{t,y})=-f^{\prime}(p_{t,y})\,p_{t,y}(1-p_{t,y})=W_{f}(p_{t,y}).</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convex versus Concave Objectives)<span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in C^{2}[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in C^{2}[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(p)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(p)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}(p)=-f^{\prime}(p)\,p(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}(p)=-f^{\prime}(p)\,p(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is concave (<math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>), then any maximizer of <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tfrac{1}{2},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tfrac{1}{2},1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is convex (<math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>), then any maximizer of <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\tfrac{1}{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\tfrac{1}{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(p)\coloneqq-f^{\prime}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(p)\coloneqq-f^{\prime}(p)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(p)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(p)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> by the hypothesis <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(p)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(p)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}(p)=s(p)\,p(1-p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}(p)=s(p)\,p(1-p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiate:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}^{\prime}(p)=s^{\prime}(p)\,p(1-p)+s(p)\,(1-2p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}^{\prime}(p)=s^{\prime}(p)\,p(1-p)+s(p)\,(1-2p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.p2.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Concave case.</em><span id="A5.p2.3.2" class="ltx_text"> If <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}(p)=-f^{\prime\prime}(p)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}(p)=-f^{\prime\prime}(p)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, hence both terms in <math id="A5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}^{\prime}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}^{\prime}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> are nonnegative; since <math id="A5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(p)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(p)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, in fact <math id="A5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}^{\prime}(p)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}^{\prime}(p)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="A5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing on <math id="A5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, so no maximizer can lie in <math id="A5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>; any global maximizer must belong to <math id="A5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tfrac{1}{2},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tfrac{1}{2},1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Convex case.</em><span id="A5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> If <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}(p)=-f^{\prime\prime}(p)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}(p)=-f^{\prime\prime}(p)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(\tfrac{1}{2},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(\tfrac{1}{2},1)</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2p&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2p&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; with <math id="A5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(p)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(p)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> the two terms in <math id="A5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}^{\prime}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}^{\prime}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> are nonpositive, hence <math id="A5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}^{\prime}(p)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}^{\prime}(p)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tfrac{1}{2},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tfrac{1}{2},1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly decreasing on <math id="A5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tfrac{1}{2},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tfrac{1}{2},1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so no maximizer can lie in <math id="A5.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tfrac{1}{2},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tfrac{1}{2},1)</annotation></semantics></math>; any global maximizer must belong to <math id="A5.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,\tfrac{1}{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\tfrac{1}{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two cases establishes the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Main Theoretical Results</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Setup and Notations</h3>

<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data model.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the input prompt <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">true</em> conditional distribution over tokens <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[V]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[V]</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>. We let <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the (marginal) distribution over pairs <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigl(x,r(\cdot\mid x)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(x,r(\cdot\mid x)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the empirical training distribution over contexts <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model and objectives.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)=\mathrm{softmax}\bigl(z_{\theta}(x)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)=\mathrm{softmax}\bigl(z_{\theta}(x)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> be the next-token distribution of an
autoregressive LM with parameters <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and write <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{0}(\cdot\mid x)=q_{\theta_{0}}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}(\cdot\mid x)=q_{\theta_{0}}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> for the base model. We note that we use different notations <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> (instead of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>) to denote the model predictions in the appendix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">population risk</em> is</p>
<table id="A6.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D},q\sim q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\Bigl[-\,\!\mathbbm{1}\{y^{*}=y^{q}\}\Bigr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D},q\sim q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\Bigl[-\,\!\mathbbm{1}\{y^{*}=y^{q}\}\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">During SFT we minimize the empirical objective</p>
<table id="A6.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f}(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(x,\tilde{y})\sim T}\bigl[f\bigl(q_{\theta}(\tilde{y}\mid x)\bigr)\bigr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f}(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{(x,\tilde{y})\sim T}\bigl[f\bigl(q_{\theta}(\tilde{y}\mid x)\bigr)\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable and decreasing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>V</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the pre-softmax logits and
<math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)=\mathrm{softmax}\bigl(z_{\theta}(x)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)=\mathrm{softmax}\bigl(z_{\theta}(x)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math> the next-token distribution.
Fix <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and suppress its dependence when clear. Define the logit feature map</p>
<table id="A6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(x,y):=\nabla_{\theta}z_{\theta_{0}}(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\qquad\Phi(x):=[\Phi(x,1),\ldots,\Phi(x,V)]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times V}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(x,y):=\nabla_{\theta}z_{\theta_{0}}(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\qquad\Phi(x):=[\Phi(x,1),\ldots,\Phi(x,V)]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times V},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and its Gram matrix over logits</p>
<table id="A6.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(x):=\Phi(x)^{\top}\Phi(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V},\qquad G_{y,y^{\prime}}(x)=\langle\Phi(x,y),\Phi(x,y^{\prime})\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(x):=\Phi(x)^{\top}\Phi(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V},\qquad G_{y,y^{\prime}}(x)=\langle\Phi(x,y),\Phi(x,y^{\prime})\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q:=q_{\theta_{0}}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:=q_{\theta_{0}}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r:=r(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:=r(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T:=T(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T:=T(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a differentiable, increasing <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, set</p>
<table id="A6.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{i})_{y}:=T_{y}\,q_{y}\,f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y}),\quad\beta_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{V},\qquad S_{f_{i}}:=\langle\beta_{i},\mathbf{1}\rangle=\sum_{y=1}^{V}T_{y}\,q_{y}\,f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>V</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>V</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{i})_{y}:=T_{y}\,q_{y}\,f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y}),\quad\beta_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{V},\qquad S_{f_{i}}:=\langle\beta_{i},\mathbf{1}\rangle=\sum_{y=1}^{V}T_{y}\,q_{y}\,f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Define the discrepancy vectors</p>
<table id="A6.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{*}:=\left(r^{\top}q\right)q-r\odot q,\qquad v_{i}:=\beta_{i}-S_{f_{i}}\,q,\qquad\beta_{12}:=\beta_{1}-\beta_{2},\;S_{12}:=S_{f_{1}}-S_{f_{2}},\;v_{12}:=v_{1}-v_{2}=\beta_{12}-S_{12}q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{*}:=\left(r^{\top}q\right)q-r\odot q,\qquad v_{i}:=\beta_{i}-S_{f_{i}}\,q,\qquad\beta_{12}:=\beta_{1}-\beta_{2},\;S_{12}:=S_{f_{1}}-S_{f_{2}},\;v_{12}:=v_{1}-v_{2}=\beta_{12}-S_{12}q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Finally, let <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}:=\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}:=\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{i}\coloneqq\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0}),g_{i}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{i}\coloneqq\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0}),g_{i}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A6.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}:=\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\,\eta\,g_{i}\bigr)\,dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}:=\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\,\eta\,g_{i}\bigr)\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">for a stepsize <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (used later in second-order expansions).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Assumptions</h3>

<section id="A6.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.2.1 </span>Main Assumptions</h4>

<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Model-Capability Assumption)<span id="Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We make the following assumptions about data capability in the Model-Strong and Model-Weak ends:</span></p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Model-Weak.</span><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> In the MW end, we assume that model predictions are uniform over the vocabulary </span><math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Model-Strong.</span><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> In the MS end, we assume that for any given </span><math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr_{y^{*},\tilde{y}}\left[(q_{y^{*}}+q_{\tilde{y}})\geq 0.55\right]\geq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.55</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{y^{*},\tilde{y}}\left[(q_{y^{*}}+q_{\tilde{y}})\geq 0.55\right]\geq K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 0.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 0.70</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span></span><span id="Thmassumption4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Trainable Base Model)<span id="Thmassumption4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume that the base model is still not perfect: for any given <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[(0.55\leq q_{y^{*}}+q_{\tilde{y}})\leq 0.95\right]\geq\alpha\Pr_{y^{*},\tilde{y}}\left[(q_{y^{*}}+q_{\tilde{y}})\leq 0.50\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.55</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[(0.55\leq q_{y^{*}}+q_{\tilde{y}})\leq 0.95\right]\geq\alpha\Pr_{y^{*},\tilde{y}}\left[(q_{y^{*}}+q_{\tilde{y}})\leq 0.50\right]</annotation></semantics></math> in the MS end.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These assumptions are mentioned in the main paper with justifications. The coefficient <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> could depend on the task itself, and this value <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> in practice. Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4 (Trainable Base Model). ‣ F.2.1 Main Assumptions ‣ F.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is a more general re-statement of Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Trainable Base Model). ‣ 5.1 Setup ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.2.2 </span>Additional Simplification Assumptions</h4>

<div id="Thmassumption5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 5</span></span><span id="Thmassumption5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Model and Data Simplifications)<span id="Thmassumption5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume that the feature matrix <math id="Thmassumption5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is preconditioned such that all of its singular values are equal to one,
and that both the training distribution <math id="Thmassumption5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and the true distribution <math id="Thmassumption5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> are one-hot.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This assumption is made purely for analytical convenience: it removes irrelevant conditioning factors in the proof and allows us to focus on the essential differences between objectives.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Main Proofs</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gradient identities)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have the following identities:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{x}\bigl[\Phi(x)\,v_{*}(x)\bigr],\qquad\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{x}\bigl[\Phi(x)\,v_{i}(x)\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{x}\bigl[\Phi(x)\,v_{*}(x)\bigr],\qquad\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{x}\bigl[\Phi(x)\,v_{i}(x)\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Population risk.</em><span id="A6.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">
With <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x}\big[-r(x)^{\top}q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x}\big[-r(x)^{\top}q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)\big]</annotation></semantics></math>,
for fixed <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathcal{R}/\partial q=-r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathcal{R}/\partial q=-r</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the chain rule through softmax,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{R}}{\partial z}=J(q)\,(-r)=(q^{\top}r)\,q-q\odot r," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{R}}{\partial z}=J(q)\,(-r)=(q^{\top}r)\,q-q\odot r,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})=\Phi(x)\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{R}}{\partial z}=\Phi(x)\,v_{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})=\Phi(x)\,\frac{\partial\mathcal{R}}{\partial z}=\Phi(x)\,v_{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking expectation over <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> yields the first identity.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">General <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>-objective.</em><span id="A6.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text">
For <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x}\big[\sum_{y}T_{y}(x)\,f_{i}(q_{y})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x}\big[\sum_{y}T_{y}(x)\,f_{i}(q_{y})\big]</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}/\partial q=m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}/\partial q=m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}=(T_{y}f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y}))_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}=(T_{y}f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y}))_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Again, <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}/\partial z=J(q)\,m_{i}=v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}/\partial z=J(q)\,m_{i}=v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
whence <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})=\Phi(x)\,v_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})=\Phi(x)\,v_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and
the claim follows after taking expectation over <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Functional derivative)<span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(f_{i})\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[v_{*}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}\Phi\,v_{i}-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}H_{i}\,\Phi\,v_{i}\right],\quad H_{i}\;:=\;\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\,\eta\,g_{i}\bigr)\,dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(f_{i})\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[v_{*}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}\Phi\,v_{i}-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}H_{i}\,\Phi\,v_{i}\right],\quad H_{i}\;:=\;\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\,\eta\,g_{i}\bigr)\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}:=\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\Phi\,v_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}:=\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\Phi\,v_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{*}:=\left(r^{\top}q\right)q-r\odot q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{*}:=\left(r^{\top}q\right)q-r\odot q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}:=\beta_{i}-S_{f_{i}}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}:=\beta_{i}-S_{f_{i}}q</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{i})_{y}:=T_{y}q_{y}f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{i})_{y}:=T_{y}q_{y}f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{f_{i}}=\sum_{y}T_{y}q_{y}f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{f_{i}}=\sum_{y}T_{y}q_{y}f_{i}^{\prime}(q_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a perturbation <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (so that <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\mapsto f_{i}+\epsilon h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\mapsto f_{i}+\epsilon h</annotation></semantics></math>), the first variation is</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta J(f_{i};h)=\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[\bigl(v_{*}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}\Phi\;-\;\eta\,v_{i}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}H_{i}\Phi\bigr)\;\delta v_{i}\right]\;+\;\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\,\int_{0}^{1}t\;\,\big\langle\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i}\bigr)\,[\delta g_{i}],\,g_{i}\otimes g_{i}\big\rangle\,dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.450em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta J(f_{i};h)=\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[\bigl(v_{*}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}\Phi\;-\;\eta\,v_{i}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}H_{i}\Phi\bigr)\;\delta v_{i}\right]\;+\;\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\,\int_{0}^{1}t\;\,\big\langle\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i}\bigr)\,[\delta g_{i}],\,g_{i}\otimes g_{i}\big\rangle\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta g_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\Phi\,\delta v_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta g_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\Phi\,\delta v_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta v_{i}\;=\;\delta\beta_{i}-(\delta S_{f_{i}})\,q\;=\;\Bigl(\mathrm{Diag}(T\odot q)-q\,(T\odot q)^{\top}\Bigr)\,h^{\prime}(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta v_{i}\;=\;\delta\beta_{i}-(\delta S_{f_{i}})\,q\;=\;\Bigl(\mathrm{Diag}(T\odot q)-q\,(T\odot q)^{\top}\Bigr)\,h^{\prime}(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=\Phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=\Phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for brevity. Then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}A\,v_{i}-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,v_{i}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}A\,v_{i}-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,v_{i}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Vary <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\mapsto f_{i}+\epsilon h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\mapsto f_{i}+\epsilon h</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}Av_{i})=v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}A\,\delta v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}Av_{i})=v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}A\,\delta v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the second term, use the product rule:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\!\left(v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,v_{i}\right)=2\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,\delta v_{i}\;+\;v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}(\delta H_{i})A\,v_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.312em;" width="0.312em"><mi>δ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\!\left(v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,v_{i}\right)=2\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,\delta v_{i}\;+\;v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}(\delta H_{i})A\,v_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta J=\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}A\,\delta v_{i}-\eta\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,\delta v_{i}-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}(\delta H_{i})A\,v_{i}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta J=\mathbb{E}_{x}\!\left[v_{*}^{\top}A^{\top}A\,\delta v_{i}-\eta\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}H_{i}A\,\delta v_{i}-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}(\delta H_{i})A\,v_{i}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}=\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i})\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}=\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i})\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A6.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\theta)=\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}(\theta)[\,\cdot\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}(\theta)=\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}(\theta)[\,\cdot\,]</annotation></semantics></math>
and the evaluation point depends on <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the chain rule yields</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta H_{i}=\int_{0}^{1}\bigl(-t\eta\bigr)\,\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i}\bigr)\,[\delta g_{i}]\,dt,\quad\text{with}\quad\delta g_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[A\,\delta v_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta H_{i}=\int_{0}^{1}\bigl(-t\eta\bigr)\,\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i}\bigr)\,[\delta g_{i}]\,dt,\quad\text{with}\quad\delta g_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[A\,\delta v_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}(\delta H_{i})A\,v_{i}=\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\int_{0}^{1}t\;\big\langle\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i}\bigr)\,[\delta g_{i}],\,Av_{i}\otimes Av_{i}\big\rangle\,dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.280em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{\eta}{2}\,v_{i}^{\top}A^{\top}(\delta H_{i})A\,v_{i}=\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\int_{0}^{1}t\;\big\langle\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}\bigl(\theta_{0}-t\eta g_{i}\bigr)\,[\delta g_{i}],\,Av_{i}\otimes Av_{i}\big\rangle\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and using trilinearity in the last two slots,
<math id="A6.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x}\langle\mathcal{T}[\delta g_{i}],Av_{i}\otimes Av_{i}\rangle=\langle\mathcal{T}[\delta g_{i}],\,(\mathbb{E}_{x}Av_{i})\otimes(\mathbb{E}_{x}Av_{i})\rangle=\langle\mathcal{T}[\delta g_{i}],\,g_{i}\otimes g_{i}\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x}\langle\mathcal{T}[\delta g_{i}],Av_{i}\otimes Av_{i}\rangle=\langle\mathcal{T}[\delta g_{i}],\,(\mathbb{E}_{x}Av_{i})\otimes(\mathbb{E}_{x}Av_{i})\rangle=\langle\mathcal{T}[\delta g_{i}],\,g_{i}\otimes g_{i}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}:=\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}:=\nabla^{3}\mathcal{R}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, gives the stated third-order term.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the variation of <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\beta_{i}=T\odot q\odot h^{\prime}(q),\qquad\delta S_{f_{i}}=\langle T\odot q,\,h^{\prime}(q)\rangle,\qquad\delta v_{i}=\delta\beta_{i}-(\delta S_{f_{i}})\,q=\Bigl(\mathrm{Diag}(T\odot q)-q\,(T\odot q)^{\top}\Bigr)h^{\prime}(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\beta_{i}=T\odot q\odot h^{\prime}(q),\qquad\delta S_{f_{i}}=\langle T\odot q,\,h^{\prime}(q)\rangle,\qquad\delta v_{i}=\delta\beta_{i}-(\delta S_{f_{i}})\,q=\Bigl(\mathrm{Diag}(T\odot q)-q\,(T\odot q)^{\top}\Bigr)h^{\prime}(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Collecting terms yields the claimed formula.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the gradient flow of the following term:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(i)})\big|_{t=0}\coloneqq\lim_{\eta\searrow 0}\frac{\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})-\mathcal{R}(\theta_{1}^{(i)})}{\eta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>↘</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(i)})\big|_{t=0}\coloneqq\lim_{\eta\searrow 0}\frac{\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})-\mathcal{R}(\theta_{1}^{(i)})}{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(i)})\big|_{t=0}=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[v_{*}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}\Phi v_{i}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(i)})\big|_{t=0}=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[v_{*}^{\top}\Phi^{\top}\Phi v_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Taylor Expansion, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})-\mathcal{R}(\theta_{1}^{(i)})=\eta\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0}),\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})\rangle-\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})^{\top}\left(\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}\left(\theta_{0}-t\eta\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}\left(\theta_{0}\right)\right)dt\right)\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0})-\mathcal{R}(\theta_{1}^{(i)})=\eta\langle\nabla\mathcal{R}(\theta_{0}),\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})\rangle-\frac{\eta^{2}}{2}\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})^{\top}\left(\int_{0}^{1}\nabla^{2}\mathcal{R}\left(\theta_{0}-t\eta\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}\left(\theta_{0}\right)\right)dt\right)\nabla\mathcal{L}_{f_{i}}(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then this corollary follows immediately from Lem. <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (Functional derivative). ‣ F.3 Main Proofs ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Useful Inequalities)<span id="Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\Delta^{V-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\Delta^{V-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability vector and fix an index <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="A6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all </span><math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A6.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}^{2}\,\|e_{j}-q\|^{2}\;\leq\;2\,q_{j}^{2}(1-q_{j})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}^{2}\,\|e_{j}-q\|^{2}\;\leq\;2\,q_{j}^{2}(1-q_{j})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the bound is tight (equality holds) when all mass </span><math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\neq j}q_{i}=1-q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\neq j}q_{i}=1-q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is concentrated on a single coordinate.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For fixed distinct </span><math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, consider</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(q)\;\coloneqq\;q_{i}q_{j}\Bigl(-q_{i}-q_{j}+\|q\|^{2}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(q)\;\coloneqq\;q_{i}q_{j}\Bigl(-q_{i}-q_{j}+\|q\|^{2}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{q\in\Delta^{V-1}}F(q)\;=\;\frac{11\sqrt{33}-59}{768}\;\leq\;0.00546," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>33</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>59</mn></mrow><mn>768</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mn> 0.00546</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{q\in\Delta^{V-1}}F(q)\;=\;\frac{11\sqrt{33}-59}{768}\;\leq\;0.00546,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the maximizer is attained by a vector with</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=q_{j}=\frac{9-\sqrt{33}}{24},\qquad\text{all remaining mass }\,1-2q_{i}\,\text{ placed on one coordinate.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>33</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">all remaining mass </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> placed on one coordinate.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=q_{j}=\frac{9-\sqrt{33}}{24},\qquad\text{all remaining mass }\,1-2q_{i}\,\text{ placed on one coordinate.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If we know </span><math id="A6.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-q_{i}-q_{j}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-q_{i}-q_{j}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-q_{i}-q_{j}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\leq 1+2(q_{i}+q_{j})^{2}-3(q_{i}+q_{j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-q_{i}-q_{j}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\leq 1+2(q_{i}+q_{j})^{2}-3(q_{i}+q_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(1)</em><span id="A6.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Since <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability vector with nonnegative coordinates,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|e_{j}-q\|^{2}=(1-q_{j})^{2}+\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}^{2}\;\leq\;(1-q_{j})^{2}+\Bigl(\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}\Bigr)^{2}\;=\;2(1-q_{j})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|e_{j}-q\|^{2}=(1-q_{j})^{2}+\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}^{2}\;\leq\;(1-q_{j})^{2}+\Bigl(\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}\Bigr)^{2}\;=\;2(1-q_{j})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">because <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}^{2}\leq(\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}^{2}\leq(\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for nonnegative terms.
Multiplying by <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> yields Eq. <a href="#A6.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Item 1 ‣ Lemma 5 (Useful Inequalities). ‣ F.3 Main Proofs ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. Equality holds when the entire mass <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> lies on a single coordinate distinct from <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}^{2}=(\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k})^{2}=(1-q_{j})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k}^{2}=(\sum_{k\neq j}q_{k})^{2}=(1-q_{j})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(2)</em><span id="A6.SS3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Set <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1-a-b\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1-a-b\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Write <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q\|^{2}=a^{2}+b^{2}+t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q\|^{2}=a^{2}+b^{2}+t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\coloneqq\sum_{k\neq i,j}q_{k}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\coloneqq\sum_{k\neq i,j}q_{k}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For fixed <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(q)=ab\bigl(-a-b+a^{2}+b^{2}+t\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(q)=ab\bigl(-a-b+a^{2}+b^{2}+t\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">is increasing in <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ab&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ab&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq s^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq s^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with equality iff all the mass <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is concentrated on a single coordinate, any maximizer (with <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ab&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ab&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) must satisfy <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=s^{2}=(1-a-b)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=s^{2}=(1-a-b)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus we may reduce to the two-variable problem</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(a,b)\;\coloneqq\;ab\Bigl(-a-b+a^{2}+b^{2}+(1-a-b)^{2}\Bigr),\qquad a\geq 0,\ b\geq 0,\ a+b\leq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≔</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(a,b)\;\coloneqq\;ab\Bigl(-a-b+a^{2}+b^{2}+(1-a-b)^{2}\Bigr),\qquad a\geq 0,\ b\geq 0,\ a+b\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is convenient to reparametrize by</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\,\coloneqq\,a+b\in[0,1],\qquad z\,\coloneqq\,(a-b)^{2}\in[0,u^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">≔</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\,\coloneqq\,a+b\in[0,1],\qquad z\,\coloneqq\,(a-b)^{2}\in[0,u^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ab=\frac{u^{2}-z}{4},\qquad a^{2}+b^{2}=\frac{u^{2}+z}{2},\qquad(1-a-b)^{2}=(1-u)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ab=\frac{u^{2}-z}{4},\qquad a^{2}+b^{2}=\frac{u^{2}+z}{2},\qquad(1-a-b)^{2}=(1-u)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">and a short calculation gives</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(u,z)\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(u^{2}-z)\Bigl(1-3u+\tfrac{3}{2}u^{2}+\tfrac{z}{2}\Bigr)\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(u^{2}-z)\bigl(K(u)+\tfrac{z}{2}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(u,z)\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(u^{2}-z)\Bigl(1-3u+\tfrac{3}{2}u^{2}+\tfrac{z}{2}\Bigr)\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(u^{2}-z)\bigl(K(u)+\tfrac{z}{2}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(u)\coloneqq 1-3u+\tfrac{3}{2}u^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(u)\coloneqq 1-3u+\tfrac{3}{2}u^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each fixed <math id="A6.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(u,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(u,z)</annotation></semantics></math> is a concave quadratic in <math id="A6.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> (its <math id="A6.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-coefficient is <math id="A6.SS3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\tfrac{1}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\tfrac{1}{8}</annotation></semantics></math>). Hence the <math id="A6.SS3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-maximizer is</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\star}(u)\;=\;\min\!\Bigl\{\,\max\!\bigl\{0,\;u^{2}-2K(u)\bigr\},\ u^{2}\Bigr\}\;=\;\min\!\Bigl\{\,\max\!\bigl\{0,\;-\alpha(u)\bigr\},\ u^{2}\Bigr\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\star}(u)\;=\;\min\!\Bigl\{\,\max\!\bigl\{0,\;u^{2}-2K(u)\bigr\},\ u^{2}\Bigr\}\;=\;\min\!\Bigl\{\,\max\!\bigl\{0,\;-\alpha(u)\bigr\},\ u^{2}\Bigr\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(u)\coloneqq u^{2}-3u+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(u)\coloneqq u^{2}-3u+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\star}(u)=\begin{cases}0,&amp;\alpha(u)\geq 0\ (\text{i.e.\ }u\in\bigl[0,\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}\bigr]),\\[2.0pt]
-\alpha(u),&amp;\alpha(u)\leq 0\ \text{and}\ u\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\ (\text{i.e.\ }u\in\bigl[\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2},\tfrac{1}{2}\bigr]),\\[2.0pt]
u^{2},&amp;u\geq\tfrac{1}{2}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>i.e. </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>i.e. </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\star}(u)=\begin{cases}0,&amp;\alpha(u)\geq 0\ (\text{i.e.\ }u\in\bigl[0,\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}\bigr]),\\[2.0pt]
-\alpha(u),&amp;\alpha(u)\leq 0\ \text{and}\ u\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\ (\text{i.e.\ }u\in\bigl[\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2},\tfrac{1}{2}\bigr]),\\[2.0pt]
u^{2},&amp;u\geq\tfrac{1}{2}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus:</span></p>
<ul id="A6.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\bigl[0,\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\bigl[0,\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\star}(u)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\star}(u)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so the maximizer over <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> occurs at <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=b=\tfrac{u}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=b=\tfrac{u}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (the symmetric point), and</p>
<table id="A6.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(u,0)=\frac{u^{2}}{4}\,K(u)=\frac{u^{2}}{4}\Bigl(1-3u+\tfrac{3}{2}u^{2}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(u,0)=\frac{u^{2}}{4}\,K(u)=\frac{u^{2}}{4}\Bigl(1-3u+\tfrac{3}{2}u^{2}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\bigl[\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2},\tfrac{1}{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\bigl[\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2},\tfrac{1}{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\star}(u)=-\alpha(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\star}(u)=-\alpha(u)</annotation></semantics></math>, and a simplification yields</p>
<table id="A6.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{z}G(u,z)=G\bigl(u,z^{\star}(u)\bigr)=\frac{(u-1)^{2}(2u-1)^{2}}{8}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>z</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{z}G(u,z)=G\bigl(u,z^{\star}(u)\bigr)=\frac{(u-1)^{2}(2u-1)^{2}}{8}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{du}\bigl[(u-1)^{2}(2u-1)^{2}/8\bigr]=\tfrac{1}{4}(u-1)(2u-1)(4u-3)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{du}\bigl[(u-1)^{2}(2u-1)^{2}/8\bigr]=\tfrac{1}{4}(u-1)(2u-1)(4u-3)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on this interval, the maximum over <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> here is attained at the left endpoint <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A6.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in[\tfrac{1}{2},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in[\tfrac{1}{2},1]</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\star}(u)=u^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\star}(u)=u^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives <math id="A6.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ab=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ab=0</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A6.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore the global maximizer must lie in the symmetric regime <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=b=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=b=x</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=2x\in[0,\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=2x\in[0,\tfrac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(x)=x^{2}\bigl(6x^{2}-6x+1\bigr),\qquad x\in\Bigl[0,\tfrac{1}{2}\Bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(x)=x^{2}\bigl(6x^{2}-6x+1\bigr),\qquad x\in\Bigl[0,\tfrac{1}{2}\Bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}(x)=2x\,(12x^{2}-9x+1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}(x)=2x\,(12x^{2}-9x+1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">so the critical point in <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12x^{2}-9x+1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12x^{2}-9x+1=0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\star}=\frac{9-\sqrt{33}}{24}\in\Bigl(0,\tfrac{1}{2}\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>33</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>24</mn></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\star}=\frac{9-\sqrt{33}}{24}\in\Bigl(0,\tfrac{1}{2}\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\tfrac{1}{2})=-\tfrac{1}{8}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\tfrac{1}{2})=-\tfrac{1}{8}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> achieves a positive value at <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, the global maximum is attained at <math id="A6.SS3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting and simplifying,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{q\in\Delta^{V-1}}F(q)=G(x_{\star})=\frac{11\sqrt{33}-59}{768}\;\leq\;0.00546." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>33</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>59</mn></mrow><mn>768</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mn> 0.00546</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{q\in\Delta^{V-1}}F(q)=G(x_{\star})=\frac{11\sqrt{33}-59}{768}\;\leq\;0.00546.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">This value is realized by</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=q_{j}=x_{\star},\qquad q_{\ell}=1-2x_{\star}\ \text{for some }\ell\notin\{i,j\},\qquad q_{k}=0\ (k\notin\{i,j,\ell\})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>for some </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=q_{j}=x_{\star},\qquad q_{\ell}=1-2x_{\star}\ \text{for some }\ell\notin\{i,j\},\qquad q_{k}=0\ (k\notin\{i,j,\ell\}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p10.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p10.6.1" class="ltx_text">i.e., the remaining mass is concentrated on a single coordinate, as established at the start.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(3)</em><span id="A6.SS3.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text"> We have that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-q_{i}-q_{j}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-q_{i}-q_{j}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-q_{i}-q_{j}+q_{i}^{2}+q_{j}^{2}+(1-q_{i}-q_{j})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-q_{i}-q_{j}+q_{i}^{2}+q_{j}^{2}+(1-q_{i}-q_{j})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1+2q_{i}^{2}+2q_{j}^{2}+2q_{i}q_{j}-3q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1+2q_{i}^{2}+2q_{j}^{2}+2q_{i}q_{j}-3q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 1+2(q_{i}+q_{j})^{2}-3(q_{i}+q_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 1+2(q_{i}+q_{j})^{2}-3(q_{i}+q_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Characterization via Gradient Flow, Restatement of Thm. <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Characterization via Gradient Flow, Informal). ‣ 5.2 Main Results ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Model-Capability Assumption). ‣ F.2.1 Main Assumptions ‣ F.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>- <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5 (Model and Data Simplifications). ‣ F.2.2 Additional Simplification Assumptions ‣ F.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, suppose that
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}(\tilde{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}(\tilde{q})</annotation></semantics></math> is negative for all <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and
that <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)(q_{\tilde{y}})&gt;-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)(q_{\tilde{y}})&gt;-c</annotation></semantics></math>
for some small positive constant <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\tilde{y})\in[0,0.55]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\tilde{y})\in[0,0.55]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)(q_{\tilde{y}})&lt;-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)(q_{\tilde{y}})&lt;-d</annotation></semantics></math> for some small positive constant <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\tilde{y})\in[0.55,0.95]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.55</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\tilde{y})\in[0.55,0.95]</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;10d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;10d</annotation></semantics></math>, with an appropriate choice of label noise ( <em id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">e.g.,</em> when <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}\neq\tilde{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}\neq\tilde{y}</annotation></semantics></math>) rate <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have the following conclusions:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A6.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}\geq\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}\geq\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
in Model Strong End.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}\leq\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}\leq\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
in Model Weak End.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption. <a href="#Thmassumption5" title="Assumption 5 (Model and Data Simplifications). ‣ F.2.2 Additional Simplification Assumptions ‣ F.2 Assumptions ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we first expand the following term:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}-\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}-\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[v_{*}^{\top}\left(v_{1}-v_{2}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[v_{*}^{\top}\left(v_{1}-v_{2}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[\left(\left(r^{\top}q\right)q-r\odot q\right)^{\top}\left(v_{12}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[\left(\left(r^{\top}q\right)q-r\odot q\right)^{\top}\left(v_{12}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{12}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y}\left[T_{y}q_{y}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{y}\right)\right]e_{y}-\left[\sum_{y}\left(T_{y}q_{y}\right)\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{y}\right)\right]q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y}\left[T_{y}q_{y}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{y}\right)\right]e_{y}-\left[\sum_{y}\left(T_{y}q_{y}\right)\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{y}\right)\right]q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex51.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)e_{\tilde{y}}-q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)e_{\tilde{y}}-q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(Only consider <math id="A6.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> one-hot)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(e_{\tilde{y}}-q\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{1}^{\prime}-f_{2}^{\prime}\right)\left(e_{\tilde{y}}-q\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can then proceeed as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}-\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}-\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\langle r\odot q-\left(r^{\top}q\right)q,e_{\tilde{y}}-q\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\langle r\odot q-\left(r^{\top}q\right)q,e_{\tilde{y}}-q\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex52.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\langle q_{y^{*}}-q_{y^{*}}q,e_{\tilde{y}}-q\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\langle q_{y^{*}}-q_{y^{*}}q,e_{\tilde{y}}-q\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<math id="A6.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is also one-hot)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\langle e_{y^{*}}-q,e_{\tilde{y}}-q\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\langle e_{y^{*}}-q,e_{\tilde{y}}-q\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left\lVert e_{y^{*}}-q\right\rVert^{2}\colon\tilde{y}=y^{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.278em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left\lVert e_{y^{*}}-q\right\rVert^{2}\colon\tilde{y}=y^{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)\colon\tilde{y}\neq y^{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)\colon\tilde{y}\neq y^{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then we first examine the weak model end, now
the model is assumed to output uniform distribution over <math id="A6.SS3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote the label noise rate to be <math id="A6.SS3.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}-\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(1)})\big|_{t=0}-\dot{\mathcal{R}}(\theta_{t}^{(2)})\big|_{t=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{V-1}{V^{3}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)\left(1-\mathcal{E}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{V-1}{V^{3}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)\left(1-\mathcal{E}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{V^{3}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{V^{3}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)\frac{1}{V^{3}}\left(\left(V-1\right)\left(1-\mathcal{E}\right)-\mathcal{E}\right)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)\frac{1}{V^{3}}\left(\left(V-1\right)\left(1-\mathcal{E}\right)-\mathcal{E}\right)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">As long as <math id="A6.SS3.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}&lt;\frac{V-1}{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}&lt;\frac{V-1}{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS3.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(\frac{1}{V}\right)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we have the desired condition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then we examine strong model end, applying Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Useful Inequalities). ‣ F.3 Main Proofs ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left\lVert e_{y^{*}}-q\right\rVert^{2}\colon\tilde{y}=y^{*}\right]\geq 2\left(1-\mathcal{E}\right)\mathbb{E}\left[\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{y^{*}}\right)q_{y^{*}}^{2}\left(1-q_{y^{*}}\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.278em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left\lVert e_{y^{*}}-q\right\rVert^{2}\colon\tilde{y}=y^{*}\right]\geq 2\left(1-\mathcal{E}\right)\mathbb{E}\left[\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{y^{*}}\right)q_{y^{*}}^{2}\left(1-q_{y^{*}}\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">and define
<math id="A6.SS3.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)(q_{\tilde{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=q_{\tilde{y}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)(q_{\tilde{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A6.SS3.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then first we show the other term is positive.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\mathcal{E}}\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)\colon\tilde{y}\neq y^{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\mathcal{E}}\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)\colon\tilde{y}\neq y^{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q\geq 0\right]+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q\geq 0\right]+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-c\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[Q\colon Q\geq 0\right]+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-c\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[Q\colon Q\geq 0\right]+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-c\Pr\left[Q\geq 0\right]*0.00546+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0.00546</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-c\Pr\left[Q\geq 0\right]*0.00546+\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p27" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the last inequality, we can proceed as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]-c\Pr\left[Q\geq 0\right]*0.00546" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0.00546</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[QR\colon Q&lt;0\right]-c\Pr\left[Q\geq 0\right]*0.00546</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq d*\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55\right]*\min_{0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55}\left\lvert Q\right\rvert-c\Pr\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\leq 0.50\right]*0.00546" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.55</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0.95</mn><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0.00546</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq d*\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55\right]*\min_{0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55}\left\lvert Q\right\rvert-c\Pr\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\leq 0.50\right]*0.00546</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=d*\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55\right]*0.045-c\Pr\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\leq 0.50\right]*0.00546" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.55</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0.045</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0.00546</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=d*\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55\right]*0.045-c\Pr\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\leq 0.50\right]*0.00546</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality comes from the sufficient condition for guaranteeing <math id="A6.SS3.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS3.p29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}&gt;0.50\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}&gt;0.50\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, and by (3) in Lem. <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Useful Inequalities). ‣ F.3 Main Proofs ‣ Appendix F Main Theoretical Results ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we have that given <math id="A6.SS3.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A6.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55}\left\lvert Q\right\rvert\leq-\max_{0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55}1+2(q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}})^{2}-3(q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}})\leq 0.045" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0.95</mn><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0.95</mn><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.55</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.045</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55}\left\lvert Q\right\rvert\leq-\max_{0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55}1+2(q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}})^{2}-3(q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}})\leq 0.045</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Also by Assumpion. <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Model-Capability Assumption). ‣ 5.1 Setup ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Trainable Base Model). ‣ 5.1 Setup ‣ 5 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Beyond Log Likelihood: Probability-Based Objectives for Supervised Fine-Tuning across the Model Capability Continuum" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have <math id="A6.SS3.p31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55\right]\geq\alpha\Pr\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\leq 0.50\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0.95</mn><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.55</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr_{\tilde{y},y^{*}}\left[0.95\geq q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\geq 0.55\right]\geq\alpha\Pr\left[q_{\tilde{y}}+q_{y^{*}}\leq 0.50\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have finished the claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, with an appropriate scale of
<math id="A6.SS3.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, specifically with
<math id="A6.SS3.p32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}&gt;\frac{\left\lvert A\right\rvert}{B-A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}&gt;\frac{\left\lvert A\right\rvert}{B-A}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.SS3.p32.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)\colon\tilde{y}\neq y^{*}\right]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left(-q_{y^{*}}-q_{\tilde{y}}+\left\lVert q\right\rVert^{2}\right)\colon\tilde{y}\neq y^{*}\right]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p32.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left\lVert e_{y^{*}}-q\right\rVert^{2}\colon\tilde{y}=y^{*}\right]&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.278em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q_{\tilde{y}}q_{y^{*}}\left(f_{2}^{\prime}-f_{1}^{\prime}\right)\left(q_{\tilde{y}}\right)\left\lVert e_{y^{*}}-q\right\rVert^{2}\colon\tilde{y}=y^{*}\right]&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then
we could achieve the desired result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
